@startuml activity_detect
' Analysing a suspect image (thesis ch. 4.4)
start
:Suspect image (upload or crawled);
:1 BLIND read (+ aspect-ratio retries);
if (Valid registered copy ID?) then (yes)
  if (content check: shows the registered picture?) then (yes)
    :verdict **watermark**;
  else (no)
    :verdict **watermark_unbound**\n(possible copy attack);
  endif
  stop
endif
:2 RETRIEVE: SIFT + RANSAC against registered originals\n(also mirrored);
if (Match with consistent structure?) then (no)
  :verdict **none**;
  stop
endif
:3 ALIGN: warp into original's frame,\nfill uncovered pixels from clean original;
:4 VERIFY: read again; BCH or match the product's codewords\n(<= limit errors at FPR 1e-6);
if (Copy verified?) then (yes)
  :verdict **watermark_aligned**;
  stop
endif
:Ownership check for every issued copy:\ninformed z vs 500 never-issued copies (z >= 4),\nDCT layer if present;
if (Our copy found?) then (yes)
  :verdict **watermark_overwritten**\n(evidence: z, copy, thief's ID, log record);
else (no)
  :verdict **fingerprint_only**;
endif
stop
@enduml
